// Coshocton County, Ohio — curated directory of meaningful links.
// Single source of truth for the app. Keep entries verified and current.
// Fields: name, category, subcategory, url, description
// Last reviewed: 2026-11-09
//
// Every URL below was fetched and its content checked against the organization
// it claims to be. Sites that block automated fetching (the Board of Elections
// and the Coshocton Tribune) were checked in a browser.
//
// THINGS THAT CHANGED SINCE JULY
//
//   * choosecoshocton.com is now a rental company's site; the Port Authority is
//     coshoctonportauthority.com.
//   * The Board of Elections is coshocton.boe.ohio.gov (boe.ohio.gov/coshocton
//     returns "page not found").
//   * The city and county health departments merged on 1 January 2023 into the
//     Coshocton Public Health District.
//   * Coshocton Regional Medical Center (Prime Healthcare) and Genesis Coshocton
//     Medical Center are two separate hospitals.
//   * Head Start is run by Coshocton County Head Start, Inc.; Community Hospice is
//     now Ohio's Hospice of New Philadelphia.
//   * The Coshocton County Beacon publishes at coshoctonbeacontoday.com.
//   * firststepcoshocton.org (the domestic violence shelter's old domain) now
//     redirects to an unrelated site.
//
// TRAPS
//
//   West Lafayette INDIANA (Purdue), Warsaw IN, Plainfield NJ/IL; a Lancaster, PA
//   "Sacred Heart" school; midohiobh.com redirects to unrelated neurology sites.
//
// GEOGRAPHY
//
//   * One city (Coshocton), villages Warsaw and West Lafayette with sites
//     (Conesville, Nellie, Plainfield do not; Baltic is mostly Tuscarawas), and
//     twenty-two townships, none with a site.
//   * The Sheriff provides law enforcement for the city by contract.
//   * The Muskingum Valley ESC (Zanesville) and the six-county mental-health board
//     (Zanesville) serve Coshocton.
//   * The solid waste district is Coshocton-Fairfield-Licking-Perry.
//   * WTNS AM/FM are licensed to Coshocton.
//
// LEFT OUT rather than listed unverified: five neighbouring-county districts (no
// first-party tie), Sacred Heart School and Interim Hospice (no first-party
// sites), the land bank, the humane society, Habitat and food pantries (no own
// sites), and WHVY (its network site never names the station).

